      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wait, this description does not make sense. Without this change any movable allocation gets ALLOC_CMA flag and __zone_watermark_ok will NOT deduct NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES(https://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v5.4.182/source/mm/page_alloc.c#L3438). After your change __zone_watermark_ok will start deducting NR_FREE_CMA_PAGES for movable allocations that don\u0027t have __GFP_CMA set.\n\nSo, the issue here is that __zone_watermark_ok thinks it has more available memory for movable allocations that don\u0027t have __GFP_CMA set and your description of the watermark check failure does not sound right. Please explain the issue you are seeing without this change.",
